# [DD-13b.W23.3] THE SHARPER HALF OF THE PAIR: `aux_arbitrary_keys.rxtin`
# catches aux being NARROWED, this one catches aux being INTERPRETED.
#
# Every key below is deliberately a REAL FORMAT KEYWORD — `pattern`, `m`,
# `provenance`, `config`, `variant` — three levels deep inside an `ext`
# body. The assertions are ABSENCES and they are the check: the file is
# accepted, and the dump contains NO extra block, NO extra case and NO
# provenance record. The colliding keys appear only as `#section aux`
# rows once W23.4 emits that section; until then they appear nowhere at
# all, which is the same claim one surface earlier.
#
# WHY THIS FIXTURE WAS RIGHT BEFORE THE RULE WAS: at revision 3.4 it
# asserted something the SPECIFICATION contradicted — S2's opener set
# ranged over siblings at any depth, so an indented `pattern` inside an
# aux body would have opened a block. The fixture was right and the rule
# was wrong, which is what produced structure-layer PARAMETER 3 (the OPEN
# SUBTREE, r58 ruling R1); this file is that parameter's first
# regression.
pattern a+
ext bench
  pattern this-is-not-a-pattern
  config
    m also-not-a-case
    provenance
      source not-a-provenance-record
      variant not-a-variant
m "aaa" 0 3
